> Acadianbun the Empiric  St:9 Dx:9 Co:17 In:7 Wi:16 Ch:18  Neutral
> Dlvl:1  $:197  HP:45(45)  Pw:38(38)  AC:-4  Exp:4

You really need to work on that strength and dexterity.
Doors are good. Lock and unlock them to exercise dexterity.
Open and shut them, when they resist, you exercise strength.
Kicking them open also exercises strength but I think doors
are often more valuable as a way to manage the battlefield
or confine a threat. When you find a boulder, push it around
a bit to exercise strength. Just spend a few extra turns
with each door and boulder and those stats will improve.
It's probably counterproductive (and boring) to spend
thousands of turns on that training.
> 
> Scrolls:  4 misc unidentified scrolls

Should have been price IDed in minetown. You can ID identify
that way as well as light and enchant weapon. The pair,
remove curse and enchant armor, can be isolated. Same for
daggers, knives and darts collected in the mines, the more
expensive the more enchanted.
> 
> Spellbooks:  healing, extra healing, stone to flesh

Stash these. Probably should have sold them for protection
money, by 20,000 turns you can get them back.
> 
> Gems:  8 misc unidentified gems, touchstone (whoop-dee-doo)

Once you can bless the touchstone you can ID the real gems
and turn them into luck or money. If you're impatient,
there's a trick with your stone to flesh spell.

